<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1189–1192</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was a military expedition by European Christian powers from 1189 to 1192, launched after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1187. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a> and, until his death on the way, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, it recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> and much of the coast. Jerusalem remained under Ayyubid control, and the war ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1192">Treaty of Jaffa</a> in 1192.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-crusade.jpg" alt="Third Crusade" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Third_Crusade_(1189-1192).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
